<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Pilgrim - ambient beds</title>
<style>
 :root { --bg:#141210; --fg:#e8e2d8; --dim:#8c8378; --line:#2e2a26; --hot:#d08b3c; --ok:#6f9f5e; }
 * { box-sizing:border-box }
 body { margin:0; padding:28px 24px 60px; background:var(--bg); color:var(--fg);
        font:14px/1.55 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; }
 h1 { font-size:18px; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 4px }
 h2 { font-size:14px; font-weight:600; margin:32px 0 4px; color:var(--hot) }
 .sub { color:var(--dim); max-width:84ch; margin:0 0 14px }
 table { border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; max-width:1180px; margin:10px 0 0 }
 th,td { text-align:right; padding:6px 9px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); white-space:nowrap }
 th { color:var(--dim); font-weight:500; font-size:11px; text-transform:uppercase;
      letter-spacing:.05em }
 td.l,th.l { text-align:left }
 tr.sel td { background:#201c18 }
 tr.run td { background:#17201a }
 button { font:inherit; color:var(--fg); background:#241f1b; border:1px solid var(--line);
          border-radius:3px; padding:4px 11px; cursor:pointer }
 button:hover { border-color:var(--hot) }
 button.on { background:var(--hot); border-color:var(--hot); color:#191511 }
 button:disabled, input:disabled { opacity:.34; cursor:default }
 button:disabled:hover { border-color:var(--line) }
 .bar { position:relative; height:28px; background:#1b1815; border:1px solid var(--line);
        border-radius:3px; max-width:1180px; margin:16px 0 8px; overflow:hidden }
 .xf { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; left:0; background:rgba(208,139,60,.22);
       border-right:1px solid var(--hot) }
 .pl { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:2px; background:var(--ok) }
 .mk { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:1px; background:rgba(232,226,216,.20) }
 input.rt { width:108px; vertical-align:middle; margin:0 7px 0 0 }
 .rv { display:inline-block; min-width:46px; text-align:right; cursor:pointer }
 .chg { color:var(--hot) }
 .stale { color:var(--dim); font-style:italic }
 .ctl { display:flex; gap:10px; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap; margin:14px 0 0 }
 .ctl label { color:var(--dim) }
 .big { font-size:13px; padding:7px 16px }
 code { color:var(--hot) }
 .note { color:var(--dim); font-size:12px; max-width:84ch }
 .gap { color:var(--dim); font-style:italic }
</style>

<h1>Ambient beds</h1>
<p class="sub">Every ambient bed in the tree, looping, at the gain its record carries, with the
cue of the duty action it belongs to firing over the top at the level the board will play it.
Built by <code>sfx_lab/generate_sound_bench.py</code> from the files on disk and the numbers in
<code>attribution.json</code> — it decodes nothing, so it runs where ffmpeg does not.</p>

<div id="rows"></div>

<h2>Levels</h2>
<p class="sub">One slider, and it moves the bed only. The cue is fixed at what the board will
play — its filed trim times the select gain — so it is the reference you set the bed against.
Use your system volume if the whole thing is too loud. <b>A bed's level is a judgement, not a
measurement:</b> a target was tried and falsified, because at equal measured loudness a bed with
voices in it sits forward of one without and no loudness measure scores that. Save writes the
levels to a JSON file; load takes one back after this page is rebuilt. Every track also carries
its own <b>trim</b> slider in the table above, which is the same number seen twice — move either
and the other follows. The row one needs no selection, so it keeps working while a whole duty
action plays, and clicking its dB figure puts the track back to the value on its record.</p>

<div class="ctl">
  <button id="play" class="big">play</button>
  <button id="seam" class="big">jump to 2.5 s before the wrap</button>
  <span style="color:var(--dim)">lap <b id="lap">0</b></span>
  <span style="color:var(--dim)"><b id="pos">0.00</b> / <b id="dur">0</b> s</span>
  <span style="color:var(--dim)">window set by <b id="win">&mdash;</b></span>
</div>

<div class="ctl">
  <label>ambient level <input id="trim" type="range" min="-40" max="6" step="0.5" value="0"
         style="width:320px"></label>
  <span id="trimdb" style="color:var(--hot)"></span>
  <span style="color:var(--dim)">&rarr; lands at <b id="lands"></b> LUFS</span>
  <button id="reset">reset to the record</button>
  <button id="save">save settings</button>
  <label style="color:var(--dim)">load <input id="load" type="file" accept=".json"
         style="width:170px"></label>
</div>

<div class="ctl">
  <button id="playall" class="big">play all of this duty action</button>
  <label>duty action level <input id="grp" type="range" min="-40" max="12" step="0.5"
         value="0" style="width:260px"></label>
  <span id="grpdb" style="color:var(--hot)"></span>
  <span style="color:var(--dim)">&rarr; the action sums to <b id="grpsum"></b> dBTP</span>
  <button id="grpreset">reset the action</button>
</div>

<p class="note" id="modenote"></p>

<div class="ctl">
  <button id="fire" class="big">fire the cue</button>
  <label><input id="rep" type="checkbox"> repeat every 6 s</label>
  <span id="cuenote" style="color:var(--dim)"></span>
</div>

<p class="sub" style="color:var(--ok)"><span id="mix">nothing sounding</span><span id="cycle"
   style="color:var(--dim)"></span></p>
<h2>Duty actions</h2>
<p class="sub">Two levels, and they do different jobs. The <b>ambient level</b> above balances
one bed against the others of its action; the <b>duty action level</b> here moves that whole
action against the others, as one gain node every track of the action feeds — so it can never
change the balance you set inside it. <b>Sums to</b> is the action's beds rendered together at
their trims and measured, not their peaks added, which on an eleven-track action reads 14 dB
high. <b>Play all</b> and the selection above are one choice and not two: starting an action
clears the selection and the ticked boxes, and clicking a track name or ticking a box stops the
action.</p>
<div id="acts"></div>
<p class="sub" id="settings" style="color:var(--ok)"></p>
<p class="sub" id="loadnote" style="color:var(--dim)"></p>

<div class="bar" id="bar">
  <div class="xf" id="xf"></div>
  <div id="mk"></div>
  <div class="pl" id="pl" style="left:0"></div>
</div>
<p class="note">The bar runs the length of the <b>longest track sounding</b>, and the faint marks
are where the shorter ones wrap inside it.</p>

<script>
var D = __DATA__;
var BEDS = D.beds, CUES = D.cues;
var ctx = null, bufs = {}, cueBufs = {}, src = null;
var master = null, bedGain = null, repTimer = null, TRIMS = {};
// TWO LEVELS. TRIMS[file] is a bed's balance against the others of its action; GDB[action] is
// where that whole action sits. They are NOT added together into one number per track: the
// group is a single gain node per action that every track of that action feeds, so it scales
// all of them by exactly the same factor and CANNOT change the balance inside the action. Add
// it into each track's gain instead and a clamp or a rounding anywhere pulls one track out of
// line -- which is the one thing a master fader must never do.
var GROUPS = D.groups || {}, GDB = {}, BUS = {};
// THE FOLDER, NOT THE CUE. `cue` is the name of a clip and is null on the four actions
// with beds and no cue filed; `action` is the folder and always exists.
function actOf(f){ var b = bed(f); return b ? b.action : null; }
function groupDb(a){ return a in GDB ? GDB[a] : 0; }
// ONE SELECTION, NOT TWO. Either a track is selected -- the transport bed plus whatever boxes
// are ticked beside it -- or a whole duty action is playing, and never both. ALL holds the
// action while play all runs and is null the rest of the time, and every control reads it, so
// there is no state in which a row is lit in the table above while eleven other tracks sound.
// The earlier version lit the action's first row, which was a true statement about which trim
// the slider would move and a false one about what you were hearing; a control that answers a
// question nobody asked, in the place reserved for the one they did, is worse than no control.
var ALL = null;
function curAction(){ return ALL ? ALL : actOf(cur); }
var cur = BEDS.length ? BEDS[0].file : null, playing = false;
var startT = 0, startOff = 0, lastPos = 0;
// A FIXED BOOST, NOT A CONTROL. Everything plays at board levels and the cues sit 20-odd dB
// under the files they came from, so without this the page is too quiet to judge. It applies
// to bed and cue alike, which is why it is not a knob: one slider, and it can only move the
// thing being decided.
var MONITOR_DB = 6;

function bed(f){ for (var i = 0; i < BEDS.length; i++) if (BEDS[i].file === f) return BEDS[i];
                 return null; }

// LAYERS SIT BESIDE THE TRANSPORT, THEY DO NOT REPLACE IT. An earlier attempt rewrote this
// page so every row had its own play button and the selected-bed transport disappeared; it
// also changed the monitor gain and added random start offsets in the same move, and when
// something sounded wrong there was no way to tell which change did it. So: the selected bed
// still plays, seeks and loops exactly as before, and a layer is an extra source that keeps
// running underneath. One rule resolves the overlap -- THE TRANSPORT WINS, so a bed that is
// selected and playing never also sounds as a layer, and can never be heard twice.
// WANT IS THE USER'S CHECKBOXES AND NOTHING ELSE. Play all does not write to it -- it clears
// it -- so there is never a tick hiding under a running action waiting to come back.
var WANT = {}, LAYERS = {};
function wantsLayer(f){
  if (ALL) return actOf(f) === ALL;
  return !!WANT[f] && !(f === cur && playing);
}
function layerStart(f, atZero){
  if (LAYERS[f] || !bufs[f]) return;
  var b = bed(f), src2 = ctx.createBufferSource(), g = ctx.createGain();
  src2.buffer = bufs[f]; src2.loop = true;
  src2.loopStart = 0; src2.loopEnd = b.seconds;   // the same pin the transport uses
  g.gain.value = Math.pow(10, TRIMS[f] / 20);
  src2.connect(g); g.connect(busFor(f));
  // START AT THE TRANSPORT'S PHASE, NOT AT THIS FILE'S ZERO. It used to be start(0), which
  // begins the layer at its own beginning whenever the box is ticked. For two independent
  // recordings that is arbitrary either way -- Allocation's 17 s howl and 28.5 s queue are
  // meant to drift. For STEMS OF ONE MIX it is wrong: Taxation's wheat, coins and creaks are
  // the same 30 s split three ways, with the coin placed to land where it lands, and ticking
  // one on mid-play would put it at a random offset against the others for the rest of the
  // session. Same length plus same phase is all the lock they need.
  // PLAY-ALL STARTS EVERY TRACK AT ITS OWN ZERO so the mix is the same every time the button
  // is pressed and a balance can be judged twice. Ticking a layer on by hand still joins at
  // the transport's phase, which is what keeps stems of one mix in step mid-play.
  src2.start(0, atZero ? 0 : (elapsed() % b.seconds));
  LAYERS[f] = {src: src2, gain: g};
}
function layerStop(f){
  var n = LAYERS[f]; if (!n) return;
  try { n.src.stop(); } catch (e) {}
  n.src.disconnect(); n.gain.disconnect(); delete LAYERS[f];
}
function syncLayers(){
  if (!ctx) return;
  BEDS.forEach(function(b){ wantsLayer(b.file) ? layerStart(b.file) : layerStop(b.file); });
  paintMix();
}
function toggleLayer(f, on){
  // A BOX IS AN INDIVIDUAL TRACK, so ticking one leaves play all for the same reason clicking a
  // row does. The action's layers go, the clock restarts, and what sounds is the boxes.
  if (ALL) exitAll();
  WANT[f] = on;
  if (!ctx) { init(function(){ syncLayers(); paintRows(); paintMode(); paintActions(); }); return; }
  syncLayers(); paintRows(); paintMode(); paintActions();
}
function sounding(){
  if (ALL) return BEDS.filter(function(b){ return b.action === ALL; });
  var out = BEDS.filter(function(b){ return wantsLayer(b.file); });
  if (playing && cur) { var c = bed(cur); if (c) out = out.concat([c]); }
  return out;
}
function gcd(a, b){ return b ? gcd(b, a % b) : a; }
function paintMix(){
  var on = sounding(), tot = 0, known = 0;
  on.forEach(function(b){
    if (b.integrated == null) return;
    known++; tot += Math.pow(10, (b.integrated + TRIMS[b.file]) / 10);
  });
  // A POWER SUM, which assumes the beds are uncorrelated -- true for different recordings.
  // Two at the same level land about 3 dB above either, so layering changes how loud an
  // action's ambience is even when no slider moved.
  document.getElementById("mix").innerHTML = on.length < 1 ? "nothing sounding"
    : on.length + (on.length === 1 ? " bed" : " beds") + " sounding" +
      (known ? ", together landing at <b>" + (10*Math.log10(tot)).toFixed(1) + "</b> LUFS" : "");
  var cyc = document.getElementById("cycle");
  if (on.length < 2) { cyc.innerHTML = ""; return; }
  var l = Math.round(on[0].seconds * 10), lock = false;
  for (var i = 1; i < on.length; i++) {
    var m = Math.round(on[i].seconds * 10);
    l = l * m / gcd(l, m);
  }
  var secs = l / 10, longest = Math.max.apply(null, on.map(function(b){ return b.seconds; }));
  lock = secs <= longest * 1.01;
  cyc.innerHTML = " &middot; this combination repeats every " + secs.toFixed(1) + " s" +
    (lock ? " <b style='color:var(--hot)'>— these lengths lock</b>" : "");
}
function dur(){ var b = bed(cur); return b ? b.seconds : 1; }
function cue(){ var b = bed(cur); return b && b.cue ? CUES[b.cue] : null; }

BEDS.forEach(function(b){ TRIMS[b.file] = b.gainDb == null ? 0 : b.gainDb; });

function b2ab(b64){
  var s = atob(b64), n = s.length, a = new Uint8Array(n);
  for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) a[i] = s.charCodeAt(i);
  return a.buffer;
}
function init(cb){
  if (ctx) { cb(); return; }
  ctx = new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)();
  master = ctx.createGain(); master.gain.value = Math.pow(10, MONITOR_DB / 20);
  master.connect(ctx.destination);
  Object.keys(GROUPS).forEach(function(a){
    var g = ctx.createGain(); g.gain.value = Math.pow(10, groupDb(a) / 20);
    g.connect(master); BUS[a] = g;
  });
  bedGain = ctx.createGain(); routeBed();
  setTrim(); setGroup();
  var ck = Object.keys(CUES), left = BEDS.length + ck.length;
  if (!left) { cb(); return; }
  BEDS.forEach(function(b){
    ctx.decodeAudioData(b2ab(b.src), function(buf){
      bufs[b.file] = buf; if (--left === 0) cb();
    }, function(){ left--; });
  });
  ck.forEach(function(k){
    ctx.decodeAudioData(b2ab(CUES[k].src), function(buf){
      cueBufs[k] = buf; if (--left === 0) cb();
    }, function(){ left--; });
  });
}
function stopSrc(){ if (src) { try { src.stop(); } catch (e) {} src.disconnect(); src = null; } }
function paintTransport(){
  var p = document.getElementById("play");
  p.textContent = playing ? "stop" : "play";
  p.classList.toggle("on", playing);
}
function rephaseLayers(){
  // A SEEK MOVES THE CLOCK AND EVERYTHING UNDER IT MOVES WITH IT, or the one number stops
  // describing the mix. Restarting is how a layer is re-phased: it joins at elapsed() % its own
  // length, which is where the clock now says it should be.
  Object.keys(LAYERS).forEach(layerStop);
  syncLayers();
}
function playFrom(off, seek){
  stopSrc();
  var b = bufs[cur]; if (!b) return;
  src = ctx.createBufferSource();
  src.buffer = b; src.loop = true;
  // PIN THE LOOP TO THE FILE'S TRUE LENGTH. Chrome's decodeAudioData hands back a few hundred
  // samples of Vorbis padding past the end -- 4 to 17 ms, near-silent on some files -- and a
  // raw loop pads every wrap with a dropout measuring 30 dB below the bed. loopEnd is in
  // seconds, which matters because the AudioContext runs at the device's rate, not the file's.
  src.loopStart = 0; src.loopEnd = dur();
  src.connect(bedGain);
  // THE CLOCK KEEPS THE WHOLE OFFSET AND THE FILE GETS IT MODULO ITS OWN LENGTH. Resuming with
  // layers already running hands back the clock's own reading, which can be past this bed's
  // length; folding it into startOff would jump the clock and silently de-phase them.
  startOff = off; startT = ctx.currentTime;
  src.start(0, off % dur());
  playing = true;
  paintTransport();
  if (seek) rephaseLayers();
  syncLayers();   // the transport has taken this bed over; drop its layer copy if it had one
}
function stopAll(){
  lastPos = elapsed(); stopSrc(); playing = false;
  paintTransport();
  syncLayers();   // handing back: a bed still ticked as a layer resumes underneath
}
// ONE CLOCK, AND EVERY SOUNDING TRACK IS AT elapsed() % ITS OWN LENGTH. The transport starts at
// startOff and a layer joins at elapsed() % its length, and that identity survives every later
// wrap, so one number gives the phase of the whole mix. It has to run whenever ANYTHING sounds
// and not only when the transport does: play all runs eleven layers and no transport at all,
// and the old clock read `playing` alone, froze at the last stop, and that is why the bar stood
// still through the one case it was most wanted for.
function anySounding(){ return playing || Object.keys(LAYERS).length > 0; }
function elapsed(){ return anySounding() ? (ctx.currentTime - startT) + startOff : lastPos; }
// THE WINDOW IS THE LONGEST THING SOUNDING, not the selected bed. With tracks of different
// lengths mixed together, "how much is left" has one honest answer -- when the longest of them
// comes round again. The shorter ones have wrapped already, several times over in places, and
// that is the point of mixing them rather than a fault; the marks in the bar say where.
function winBed(){
  var on = sounding(), best = null;
  on.forEach(function(b){ if (!best || b.seconds > best.seconds) best = b; });
  return best || bed(cur);
}
function winLen(){ var b = winBed(); return b && b.seconds > 0 ? b.seconds : 1; }
function posNow(){ return elapsed() % winLen(); }

function fireCue(){
  var c = cue(); if (!c || !ctx || !cueBufs[bed(cur).cue]) return;
  var s = ctx.createBufferSource(), g = ctx.createGain();
  s.buffer = cueBufs[bed(cur).cue];
  g.gain.value = Math.pow(10, (c.gainDb || 0) / 20) * c.role;
  s.connect(g); g.connect(master); s.start(0);
}
function busFor(f){ var a = actOf(f); return (a && BUS[a]) ? BUS[a] : master; }
function routeBed(){
  if (!bedGain) return;
  try { bedGain.disconnect(); } catch (e) {}
  bedGain.connect(busFor(cur));
}
function setGroup(){
  // THE ACTION THAT IS SOUNDING, not the action of an invisible pointer. While play all runs
  // nothing is selected, and this slider is the one control that still has an obvious subject.
  var a = curAction();
  var v = +document.getElementById("grp").value;
  if (a) GDB[a] = v;
  document.getElementById("grpdb").textContent =
      (v >= 0 ? "+" : "−") + Math.abs(v).toFixed(1) + " dB";
  var g = a ? GROUPS[a] : null;
  var sum = (g && g.summedTruePeakDbtp != null) ? g.summedTruePeakDbtp + v : null;
  // THE SUM SCALES EXACTLY WITH THE BUS, so one rendered figure plus the group level is the
  // true answer rather than a bound. Adding the tracks' individual peaks instead reads 14 dB
  // high on Build Roads, which is why that number is not used here.
  document.getElementById("grpsum").innerHTML = sum == null ? "&mdash;"
      : (sum >= 0 ? "+" : "−") + Math.abs(sum).toFixed(2) +
        (sum > -1 ? " <b style='color:var(--hot)'>over the cue ceiling</b>" : "");
  if (a && BUS[a]) BUS[a].gain.value = Math.pow(10, v / 20);
  paintSettings();
}
// ONE PLACE WHERE A TRIM REACHES THE AUDIO, whichever control moved it. A track can be sounding
// through the transport, through a layer, or through neither, and before this there were two
// copies of the rule, one of which was about to become three.
function applyTrim(f){
  var g = Math.pow(10, TRIMS[f] / 20);
  if (LAYERS[f]) LAYERS[f].gain.gain.value = g;
  if (f === cur && bedGain) bedGain.gain.value = g;
}
function setTrim(){
  var t = +document.getElementById("trim").value;
  TRIMS[cur] = t;
  document.getElementById("trimdb").textContent =
      (t >= 0 ? "+" : "−") + Math.abs(t).toFixed(1) + " dB";
  var b = bed(cur), lands = b && b.integrated != null ? b.integrated + t : null;
  document.getElementById("lands").innerHTML = lands == null ? "&mdash;"
      : (lands < 0 ? "−" : "") + Math.abs(lands).toFixed(1);
  applyTrim(cur); paintRowTrim(cur);
  paintSettings(); paintMix();
}
// THE TWO CONTROLS ARE ONE NUMBER SEEN TWICE, so each writes TRIMS and then repaints the other.
// They are not two settings to reconcile: whichever you touch, the row and the big slider read
// the same afterwards, and nothing is stored in a widget's value.
function rowTrim(f, v){
  TRIMS[f] = v;
  applyTrim(f);
  if (f === cur) {
    document.getElementById("trim").value = v;
    document.getElementById("trimdb").textContent =
        (v >= 0 ? "+" : "−") + Math.abs(v).toFixed(1) + " dB";
    var b = bed(cur), l = b && b.integrated != null ? b.integrated + v : null;
    document.getElementById("lands").innerHTML = l == null ? "&mdash;"
        : (l < 0 ? "−" : "") + Math.abs(l).toFixed(1);
  }
  paintRowTrim(f);
  queueRepaint();
}
function rowReset(f){
  var b = bed(f); if (!b) return;
  rowTrim(f, b.gainDb == null ? 0 : b.gainDb);
}
// REPAINTS ARE COALESCED TO ONE A FRAME. Dragging a row slider fires on every pixel, and the
// settings line and the duty-action table are both full innerHTML rebuilds; the audio and the
// row's own readout are done immediately, and the rest catches up at the next frame.
var repaintQ = 0;
function queueRepaint(){
  if (repaintQ) return;
  repaintQ = requestAnimationFrame(function(){ repaintQ = 0; paintSettings(); paintMix(); });
}
function paintRowTrim(f){
  var b = bed(f); if (!b) return;
  var t = TRIMS[f], filed = b.gainDb == null ? 0 : b.gainDb;
  var s = document.getElementById("rt_" + b.id);
  if (s && +s.value !== t) s.value = t;
  var v = document.getElementById("rv_" + b.id);
  if (v) {
    v.textContent = (t >= 0 ? "+" : "−") + Math.abs(t).toFixed(1);
    v.className = "rv" + (Math.abs(t - filed) > 0.01 ? " chg" : "");
  }
  var l = document.getElementById("rl_" + b.id);
  if (l) l.innerHTML = b.integrated == null ? "&mdash;" : (b.integrated + t).toFixed(1);
}
function paintRowTrims(){ BEDS.forEach(function(b){ paintRowTrim(b.file); }); }
function paintSettings(){
  document.getElementById("settings").innerHTML = "levels &mdash; " + BEDS.map(function(b){
    var t = TRIMS[b.file];
    return b.name + " " + (t >= 0 ? "+" : "−") + Math.abs(t).toFixed(1) + " dB" +
      (b.integrated == null ? "" : " (" + (b.integrated + t).toFixed(1) + " LUFS)") +
      (Math.abs(t - (b.gainDb == null ? 0 : b.gainDb)) > 0.01 ? " <b>changed</b>" : "");
  }).join(" &middot; ");
  paintActions();
}
function paintCue(){
  var c = cue();
  document.getElementById("fire").textContent = c ? "fire the " + c.name + " cue" : "no cue";
  document.getElementById("fire").disabled = !c;
  document.getElementById("cuenote").innerHTML = c
    ? "cue at its filed trim " + (c.gainDb > 0 ? "+" : "−") +
      Math.abs(c.gainDb).toFixed(1) + " dB × the board's <b>select</b> gain " +
      c.role.toFixed(2)
    : "this bed's duty action has no cue filed, so there is nothing to set it against";
}
function pick(f){
  // SELECTING A TRACK LEAVES PLAY ALL, it does not join it. The action's layers go, and what is
  // left sounding is this track plus whatever boxes are ticked -- which, straight after a play
  // all, is none of them, because play all cleared them on the way in. Picking from a running
  // action starts this track playing rather than selecting it silently: the page was making
  // sound a moment ago and going quiet on a click would read as a fault.
  var wasAll = !!ALL, e = elapsed();
  if (wasAll) { exitAll(); e = 0; }
  cur = f;
  routeBed();
  document.getElementById("trim").value = TRIMS[cur];
  document.getElementById("grp").value = groupDb(curAction());
  if (wasAll) playFrom(0, true);
  else if (playing) playFrom(e);
  setTrim(); setGroup(); paintCue(); syncLayers();
  paintRows(); paintMode(); paintActions();
}
function exitAll(){
  if (!ALL) return;
  ALL = null;
  Object.keys(LAYERS).forEach(layerStop);
  startOff = 0; lastPos = 0; if (ctx) startT = ctx.currentTime;
}
function playAll(a){
  if (ALL === a) {   // the lit button is the way out
    exitAll(); paintRows(); paintMode(); paintActions(); paintMix(); return;
  }
  // THE TRANSPORT AND THE TICKED BOXES BOTH GO. Play all is the other selection and not a layer
  // on top of this one. Leaving the transport running would put one track at its phase while
  // the rest start at zero -- the mix would differ every time the button was pressed, and a
  // balance you cannot hear twice is not a balance. Clearing the boxes rather than remembering
  // them is the same rule seen from the other side: nothing comes back from underneath when the
  // action stops, because nothing was hidden under it.
  init(function(){
    stopSrc(); playing = false; paintTransport();
    Object.keys(LAYERS).forEach(layerStop);
    WANT = {}; clearBoxes();
    ALL = a;
    startOff = 0; lastPos = 0; startT = ctx.currentTime;
    BEDS.forEach(function(b){ if (b.action === a) layerStart(b.file, true); });
    document.getElementById("grp").value = groupDb(a);
    setGroup(); paintRows(); paintMode(); paintActions(); paintMix();
  });
}
function clearBoxes(){
  BEDS.forEach(function(b){
    var e = document.getElementById("ly_" + b.id); if (e) e.checked = false; });
}
function paintRows(){
  document.querySelectorAll("tr[data-f]").forEach(function(tr){
    var f = tr.getAttribute("data-f");
    tr.classList.toggle("sel", !ALL && f === cur);
    tr.classList.toggle("run", !!ALL && actOf(f) === ALL);
  });
  document.querySelectorAll("button[data-f]").forEach(function(b){
    b.classList.toggle("on", !ALL && b.getAttribute("data-f") === cur); });
}
function paintMode(){
  var off = !!ALL;
  ["trim", "reset", "play", "seam", "fire", "rep"].forEach(function(id){
    var e = document.getElementById(id); if (e) e.disabled = off; });
  var pa = document.getElementById("playall");
  pa.textContent = off ? "stop playing all" : "play all of this duty action";
  pa.classList.toggle("on", off);
  var g = off ? (GROUPS[ALL] || {}) : null;
  document.getElementById("modenote").innerHTML = !off ? "" :
    "<b style='color:var(--ok)'>" + (g.duty || ALL) + "</b> is playing, all " + (g.tracks || "") +
    " tracks of it, so no single track is selected and the controls that need one are off. " +
    "Balance them with the <b>trim</b> column in the table above, which needs no selection and " +
    "stays live; the duty action level here still moves the whole action. Click any " +
    "track&rsquo;s name, or tick any box, to leave and go back to one track at a time.";
}
function paintActions(){
  var acts = Object.keys(GROUPS).sort();
  document.getElementById("acts").innerHTML =
    "<table><tr><th class='l'>duty action</th><th>tracks</th><th></th><th>group</th>" +
    "<th>sums to</th></tr>" + acts.map(function(a){
      var g = GROUPS[a], v = groupDb(a);
      var sum = g.summedTruePeakDbtp == null ? null : g.summedTruePeakDbtp + v;
      // THE SUM WAS RENDERED AT THE FILED TRIMS AND SAYS SO WHEN THEY MOVE. It is a measurement
      // of eleven files mixed together, not a figure this page can recompute -- adding their
      // peaks reads 14 dB high. Move a trim and it is a measurement of something else; the only
      // honest thing the page can do is stop presenting it as current.
      var dirty = BEDS.some(function(b){
        return b.action === a &&
               Math.abs(TRIMS[b.file] - (b.gainDb == null ? 0 : b.gainDb)) > 0.01; });
      var here = (a === ALL);
      return "<tr" + (a === curAction() ? (here ? " class='run'" : " class='sel'") : "") +
        "><td class='l'>" + (g.duty || a) + "</td><td>" + g.tracks + "</td>" +
        "<td><button onclick=\"playAll('" + a + "')\"" +
          (here ? " class='on'" : "") + ">" + (here ? "stop" : "play all") + "</button></td>" +
        "<td>" + (v >= 0 ? "+" : "−") + Math.abs(v).toFixed(1) +
          (Math.abs(v - (g.groupDb || 0)) > 0.01 ? " <b>changed</b>" : "") + "</td>" +
        "<td" + (sum != null && sum > -1 && !dirty ? " style='color:var(--hot)'" : "") + ">" +
          (sum == null ? "&mdash;"
           : dirty ? "<span class='stale'>" + sum.toFixed(2) + " at the filed trims</span>"
           : sum.toFixed(2) + " dBTP") + "</td></tr>";
    }).join("") + "</table>";
}
document.getElementById("play").onclick = function(){
  if (playing) { stopAll(); return; }
  // RESUME ONTO THE RUNNING CLOCK if layers are already sounding, rather than onto the stale
  // reading taken when the transport last stopped -- which would jump the clock out from under
  // them and de-phase every one.
  init(function(){ playFrom(anySounding() ? elapsed() : lastPos); });
};
document.getElementById("seam").onclick = function(){
  init(function(){ playFrom(Math.max(0, dur() - 2.5), true); });
};
document.getElementById("trim").oninput = setTrim;
document.getElementById("grp").oninput = setGroup;
document.getElementById("playall").onclick = function(){
  if (ALL) { playAll(ALL); return; }   // playAll toggles when handed the action already running
  var a = actOf(cur); if (a) playAll(a);
};
document.getElementById("grpreset").onclick = function(){
  var a = curAction(); if (!a) return;
  document.getElementById("grp").value = GROUPS[a].groupDb || 0; setGroup(); paintActions();
};
document.getElementById("reset").onclick = function(){
  var b = bed(cur);
  document.getElementById("trim").value = b.gainDb == null ? 0 : b.gainDb; setTrim();
};
document.getElementById("fire").onclick = function(){ init(fireCue); };
document.getElementById("rep").onchange = function(){
  if (repTimer) { clearInterval(repTimer); repTimer = null; }
  if (this.checked) init(function(){ fireCue(); repTimer = setInterval(fireCue, 6000); });
};
// WHAT GETS SAVED IS WHAT THE RECORD NEEDS. A trim on its own cannot be checked later; with
// the measured loudness and the true peak beside it, both the resulting level and the ceiling
// check can be re-derived from the file without this page.
document.getElementById("save").onclick = function(){
  var out = {savedAt: new Date().toISOString(), page: "ambient_bench", monitorDb: MONITOR_DB,
    beds: BEDS.map(function(b){
      var t = TRIMS[b.file];
      // trimDb IS THE TRACK'S OWN NUMBER AND NEVER THE SUM. The group level is saved once
      // per action below. Write the total here and a reload would apply the group twice --
      // the file would be silently 2x the level it described, and nothing would say so.
      var gd = groupDb(b.action);
      return {file: b.file, name: b.name, duty: b.duty, action: b.action,
              trimDb: +t.toFixed(1), groupDb: +gd.toFixed(1),
              effectiveDb: +(t + gd).toFixed(1),
              recordGainDb: b.gainDb, integratedLufs: b.integrated,
              landsAtLufs: b.integrated == null ? null : +(b.integrated + t + gd).toFixed(2),
              truePeakDbtp: b.tp,
              truePeakAfterTrimDbtp: b.tp == null ? null : +(b.tp + t + gd).toFixed(2)};
    }),
    groups: Object.keys(GROUPS).sort().map(function(a){
      var g = GROUPS[a], v = groupDb(a);
      return {action: a, duty: g.duty, tracks: g.tracks, groupDb: +v.toFixed(1),
              recordGroupDb: g.groupDb,
              summedTruePeakDbtp: g.summedTruePeakDbtp,
              summedAfterGroupDbtp: g.summedTruePeakDbtp == null ? null
                                    : +(g.summedTruePeakDbtp + v).toFixed(2)};
    })};
  var blob = new Blob([JSON.stringify(out, null, 1)], {type: "application/json"});
  var u = URL.createObjectURL(blob), a = document.createElement("a");
  a.href = u; a.download = "ambient_levels.json";
  document.body.appendChild(a); a.click(); a.remove();
  setTimeout(function(){ URL.revokeObjectURL(u); }, 2000);
};
document.getElementById("load").onchange = function(){
  var f = this.files && this.files[0]; if (!f) return;
  var r = new FileReader();
  r.onload = function(){
    try {
      var j = JSON.parse(r.result), n = 0, gn = 0;
      (j.beds || []).forEach(function(b){
        var k = b.file in TRIMS ? b.file : null;
        if (k) { TRIMS[k] = b.trimDb; n++; }
      });
      // A FILE SAVED BEFORE THE GROUP LEVEL EXISTED HAS NO `groups`, and must still load. It
      // leaves the group levels alone rather than zeroing them, because absent is not the
      // same as zero and silently flattening an action is worse than ignoring an old file.
      (j.groups || []).forEach(function(g){
        if (g.action in GROUPS) { GDB[g.action] = g.groupDb; gn++; }
      });
      Object.keys(BUS).forEach(function(a){
        BUS[a].gain.value = Math.pow(10, groupDb(a) / 20); });
      // EVERY TRACK ALREADY SOUNDING TAKES ITS NEW TRIM TOO. setTrim only reaches the selected
      // bed, and under play all there is no selected bed and eleven layers -- loading a file
      // would have moved the numbers on the page and nothing in the air.
      BEDS.forEach(function(b){ applyTrim(b.file); });
      document.getElementById("trim").value = TRIMS[cur];
      document.getElementById("grp").value = groupDb(curAction());
      setTrim(); setGroup(); paintRowTrims(); paintRows(); paintMode(); paintActions();
      var extra = (j.beds || []).length - n;
      document.getElementById("loadnote").textContent = "restored " + n +
        (n === 1 ? " level" : " levels") + " and " + gn +
        (gn === 1 ? " duty action" : " duty actions") + " from " + f.name +
        (extra > 0 ? " (" + extra + " in the file are not on this page)" : "") +
        (j.groups ? "" : " — no group levels in that file, the ones here are unchanged");
    } catch (e) {
      document.getElementById("loadnote").textContent = "could not read " + f.name;
    }
  };
  r.readAsText(f);
};
var markSig = "";
function paintMarks(d){
  // REBUILT ONLY WHEN THE SET CHANGES, not sixty times a second. The signature is the window
  // length and the files in it, which is exactly what the marks depend on.
  var on = sounding();
  var sig = d.toFixed(3) + "|" + on.map(function(b){ return b.file; }).sort().join(",");
  if (sig === markSig) return;
  markSig = sig;
  var h = [];
  on.forEach(function(b){
    if (!(b.seconds > 0.05) || b.seconds >= d - 0.001) return;
    if (d / b.seconds > 200) return;
    for (var t = b.seconds; t < d - 0.001; t += b.seconds)
      h.push("<div class='mk' style='left:" + (100 * t / d).toFixed(3) + "%'></div>");
  });
  document.getElementById("mk").innerHTML = h.join("");
}
function tick(){
  var wb = winBed(), d = winLen(), p = elapsed() % d;
  document.getElementById("pos").textContent = p.toFixed(2);
  document.getElementById("dur").textContent = d.toFixed(1);
  document.getElementById("win").textContent = wb ? wb.name : "—";
  document.getElementById("lap").textContent = Math.floor(elapsed() / d);
  document.getElementById("pl").style.left = (100 * p / d) + "%";
  document.getElementById("xf").style.width = (100 * 1.5 / d) + "%";
  paintMarks(d);
  requestAnimationFrame(tick);
}

(function build(){
  var h = ["<h2>" + D.have + " of " + D.slots + " duty actions have a bed</h2>"];
  if (!BEDS.length) {
    h.push("<p class='sub gap'>No ambient beds in sfx/ambient/ yet.</p>");
    document.getElementById("rows").innerHTML = h.join("");
    return;
  }
  // THE TRIM COLUMN IS THE ONE CONTROL THAT NEEDS NO SELECTION, which is the whole reason it
  // exists. Selecting a track and playing a whole duty action are one choice and not two, so
  // the big slider above has no subject while an action plays -- and balancing eleven tracks
  // against each other is exactly the job you want doing while all eleven sound. A number
  // edited in place asks for no selection, so it stays live in every mode and breaks nothing.
  // `filed` beside it is the record's own gainDb and never moves: the anchor to come back to.
  h.push("<table><tr><th class='l'>bed</th><th>layer</th><th class='l'>trim</th>" +
         "<th class='l'>duty action</th><th>length</th>" +
         "<th>rate</th><th>ch</th><th>integrated</th><th>true peak</th><th>filed</th>" +
         "<th>lands</th><th>size</th></tr>");
  BEDS.forEach(function(b){
    var t0 = b.gainDb == null ? 0 : b.gainDb;
    h.push("<tr data-f='" + b.file + "'><td class='l'><button data-f='" + b.file +
      "' onclick=\"pick('" + b.file + "')\">" + b.name + "</button></td>" +
      "<td><input type='checkbox' id='ly_" + b.id + "' onchange=\"toggleLayer('" + b.file +
        "', this.checked)\" title='keep this bed looping underneath whatever is selected — " +
        "ticking one while a duty action is playing stops that action'></td>" +
      "<td class='l'><input type='range' class='rt' id='rt_" + b.id + "' min='-40' max='6' " +
        "step='0.5' value='" + t0 + "' oninput=\"rowTrim('" + b.file + "', +this.value)\" " +
        "title='this track&#39;s own level — it moves nothing else, and stays live while a " +
        "whole duty action is playing'>" +
        "<span class='rv' id='rv_" + b.id + "' onclick=\"rowReset('" + b.file + "')\" " +
        "title='click to restore the filed value'></span></td>" +
      "<td class='l' style='color:var(--dim)'>" + (b.duty || "&mdash;") + "</td>" +
      "<td>" + (b.ms / 1000).toFixed(0) + " s</td><td>" + b.sr + "</td><td>" +
      (b.ch === 1 ? "mono" : b.ch + " ch") + "</td>" +
      "<td>" + (b.integrated == null ? "&mdash;" : b.integrated.toFixed(2)) + "</td>" +
      "<td>" + (b.tp == null ? "&mdash;" : b.tp.toFixed(2)) + "</td>" +
      "<td>" + (b.gainDb == null ? "<span class=gap>none</span>"
                : (b.gainDb > 0 ? "+" : "−") + Math.abs(b.gainDb).toFixed(1)) + "</td>" +
      // LANDS FOLLOWS THE LIVE TRIM, not the filed one. It is the only number on the row that
      // answers "where is it now", and a stale one beside a slider you are dragging is worse
      // than none -- it would be read as the answer.
      "<td id='rl_" + b.id + "'>&mdash;</td>" +
      "<td>" + Math.round(b.bytes / 1024) + " KB</td></tr>");
  });
  h.push("</table>");
  D.missing.forEach(function(m){
    h.push("<p class='sub gap'>" + m + " has no bed</p>");
  });
  document.getElementById("rows").innerHTML = h.join("");
  BEDS.forEach(function(b){ if (!(b.action in GDB)) GDB[b.action] = (GROUPS[b.action] || {}).groupDb || 0; });
  pick(cur); paintRowTrims(); paintActions(); tick();
})();
</script>
